  "notes": [
    "Per-minute list rates for GitHub-hosted Actions runners, copied from GitHub's 'Actions runner pricing' reference (source above), read 2026-10-12. The baseline rows also appear, with the same figures, on https://docs.github.com/en/billing/concepts/product-billing/github-actions, read the same day.",
    "Rounding: 'GitHub rounds the minutes and partial minutes each job uses up to the nearest whole minute' (actions-runner-pricing, read 2026-10-12). Each job is rounded on its own, then multiplied by its SKU's rate.",
    "Platform charge: GitHub's changelog of 2025-12-16 (https://github.blog/changelog/2025-12-16-coming-soon-simpler-pricing-and-a-better-experience-for-github-actions/, read 2026-10-12) says of the hosted rates effective 2026-01-01: 'These listed rates include the new $0.002 per-minute Actions cloud platform charge.' Nothing is added on top of the rates below. The reference page itself does not mention the charge.",
    "Public repositories: 'GitHub Actions usage is free for self-hosted runners and for public repositories that use standard GitHub-hosted runners' and 'Larger runners are always charged for, even when used by public repositories' (product-billing/github-actions, read 2026-10-12). Rows with larger=true are the larger runners; every other row is a standard runner.",
    "Self-hosted runners: the billing page read 2026-10-12 says their usage is free. The same changelog says 'We're postponing the announced billing change for self-hosted GitHub Actions to take time to re-evaluate our approach.' A self-hosted job is never priced here: it is reported as unpriced (self_hosted), not as $0.",
    "Included minutes: a private repository's plan includes free minutes for standard runners (2,000 a month on GitHub Free, 3,000 on Pro and Team, 50,000 on Enterprise Cloud, per product-billing/github-actions, read 2026-10-12). A job cannot know how much of the owner's allowance is left, so a job's figure is its list price before the allowance: an estimate, labelled so.",
    "labels maps the workflow labels GitHub documents for standard runners (https://docs.github.com/en/actions/reference/runners/github-hosted-runners, private-repository table) and for macOS larger runners (https://docs.github.com/en/actions/reference/runners/larger-runners), both read 2026-10-12, to a SKU. Linux and Windows larger runners carry a name their owner chose; one is priced only when that name states the OS and the core count (for example ubuntu-latest-4-cores, linux-8-core-arm) and the SKU it spells exists here. Any other label is unpriced, never guessed."
  ],
